-- title:
--   Section prime at the width-two supersingular node j = 1728
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$; assume $1728 \in$ `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $1728$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Let $K \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a number field, write $A_K = A \cap K$ for `coeffSubring A K` and let $\mathrm{red}_K$ be the induced map $A_K \to k$; let $\varpi \in A_K$ be such that $\ker \mathrm{red}_K$ is the set of multiples of $\varpi$, and suppose $q = \varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$ with $\varepsilon$ a unit and $e_K \ge 1$. Let $R$ be `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A_K red_K 1728 (1728 ^ q)`, the subring of Laurent series $f$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ admitting $f \cdot \mathrm{modularEval}(s) = \mathrm{modularEval}(r)$ with $r, s \in A_K[X_0, X_1]$ and $\mathrm{pointEval}(s) \ne 0$, where $\mathrm{modularEval}$ sends $X_0 \mapsto j(\mathsf{q})$, $X_1 \mapsto j(\mathsf{q}^{q})$ and coefficients to constant series, and $\mathrm{pointEval}$ reduces coefficients by $\mathrm{red}_K$ and sends $(X_0, X_1) \mapsto (1728, 1728^{q})$. Let $\tilde\varpi \in R$ be the image of the constant $\varpi$, and let $G', H', w \in R$ with $w$ a unit satisfy the crossing presentation $G'H' = \tilde\varpi^{\,\mathrm{jWidth}(1728)\,e_K} w$ (the width being $2$ here, as $1728 \ne 0$ in $k$); assume further that, whenever $R$ is local, its maximal ideal is $(\tilde\varpi, G', H')$, that $(\tilde\varpi, G')$ and $(\tilde\varpi, H')$ are prime with $H' \notin (\tilde\varpi, G')$ and $G' \notin (\tilde\varpi, H')$, and that $(\tilde\varpi, G') = (\tilde\varpi, \mathrm{modularEval}(X_1 - X_0^{q}))$ and $(\tilde\varpi, H') = (\tilde\varpi, \mathrm{modularEval}(X_0 - X_1^{q}))$. Let $c$ lie in the maximal ideal of $A$ and be admissible, in the sense that $c\,m = q^{2}$ for some $m$ in that maximal ideal, and let $K' \supseteq K$ be a number field with $c \in K'$. Then the Laurent series $G'$ lies in `fieldOver (1 * q) K'`, the subfield generated by the constant series of $K'$ together with $j(\mathsf{q})$ and $j(\mathsf{q}^{q})$, and the ring $C' =$ `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K'` of elements of that subfield integral over the subring generated by the constant series of $A \cap K'$ and $j(\mathsf{q})$ carries a prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of height $1$ with $q \notin \mathfrak{p}$, such that every $s \in (A\cap K')[X_0, X_1]$ with $\mathrm{pointEval}(s) \ne 0$ at $(1728, 1728^{q})$ has $\mathrm{modularEval}(s) \notin \mathfrak{p}$ whenever it lies in $C'$, and such that there are $r_0, r, s \in C'$ with $s \notin \mathfrak{p}$, $r \in \mathfrak{p}$, $G's = r_0$, $(G' - c)s = r$, $r \ne 0$, and every $t \in \mathfrak{p}$ satisfies $tv = ru$ for some $u, v \in C'$ with $v \notin \mathfrak{p}$.
--
--   This is the algebraisation step for the width-two supersingular node $j = 1728$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(q)$: given a crossing presentation of the node ring over $A \cap K$ and an admissible value $c$ of the crossing parameter $G'$ (one with $|q|^{2} < |c| < 1$), it produces a height-one prime of the normal model over a number field containing $c$ at which $G' \equiv c$ and at which $G' - c$ generates the prime after localisation. It is used for the existence half of the statement that such a place is unique ([`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.existsUnique_place_centred_ofNat1728_hasValue_of_crossingPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.existsUnique_place_centred_ofNat1728_hasValue_of_crossingPresentation)) and for the uniformiser law [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.ord_sub_eq_one_of_centred_ofNat1728_of_crossingPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.ord_sub_eq_one_of_centred_ofNat1728_of_crossingPresentation).
